  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian response for families affected by fire in Quibdo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">43 Afro-Colombian families lost their homes in Quibd&#xf3; as a result of a fire on 5th December 2022. The families are made up of 136 people, of whom 87 are adults: 48 adult women, 39 adult men, 12 adult men and women and 49 minors. These families are victims of armed conflict, who were forced to flee their homes due to the armed conflict during the 2000s. They built some temporary housing, but lost everything with the fire. This project supported Pastoral Social Quibd&#xf3; in coordination with the parish, members of the Community Action  Councils (JAC) and social leaders, to deliver humanitarian aid consisting of 43 food kits and  hygiene kits..</narrative>
  </description>
